      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q6-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) From dh/dt = −Ah1/2, write dh = −Ah1/2dt, divide by h1/2, and integrate: Z Z h−1/2 dh = −A dt. √ √ This gives 2 h = C −At. [M1] From h(0) = 100 [A1] we get 2 100 = C, so C = 20, and h(2) = 64 √ √ [A1] gives 16 = 20 −2A, [A1] so A = 2. [A1] Now 2 h = 20 −2t, so h = 10 −t. The hole is at h = 1. [A1] Then 1 = 10 −t, [A1] so the leak stops at t = 9 minutes . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
