    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"It is given that 3 cos3 x ≡ 4cos x − 3cos x . a) Prove the validity of the above trigonometric identity. ( ) 5 b) Hence, or otherwise solve the trigonometric equation ( ) 7 2 + cos6 sec2 θ θ = 0 , 0 ° ≤ θ &lt; 360 ° .\" style=\"--madas-width:589.5px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The addition and double-angle formulae give cos 3x = cos(2x + x) = cos 2x cos x −sin 2x sin x = (2 cos2 x −1) cos x −(2 sin x cos x) sin x = 2 cos3 x −cos x −2 sin2 x cos x = (2 cos2 x −1) cos x −2(1 −cos2 x) cos x = 2 cos3 x −cos x −2 cos x + 2 cos3 x = 4 cos3 x −3 cos x. [M1] Use the cosine addition formula [M1] expand the double-angle cosine [M1] expand the double-angle sine [M1] use the Pythagorean identity [A1] collect the cubic and linear terms (b) Here cos 2θ̸ = 0. [B1] Substitute\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q8-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"cos 6θ = cos(3 × 2θ) = 4 cos3 2θ −3 cos 2θ 2 + cos 6θ sec 2θ = 0 2 + [4 cos3 2θ −3 cos 2θ] sec 2θ = 0 2 + 4 cos3 2θ sec 2θ −3 cos 2θ sec 2θ = 0 2 + 4 cos2(2θ) −3 = 0 Applying part (a) at x = 2θ gives 4 cos2 2θ −1 = 0. Using cos2(2θ) = (1 + cos 4θ)/2 gives 1 2 + 1  4 2 cos 4θ = 1 2 + 2 cos 4θ = 1 2 cos 4θ = −1 cos 4θ = −1 2\" style=\"--madas-width:488.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q8-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"In one turn 4θ = 120◦or 240◦. Hence cos 4θ = −1/2. [A1] This gives θ = 30◦+ 90◦n [A1] or 60◦+ 90◦n. The solutions are 30◦, 60◦, 120◦, 150◦, 210◦, 240◦, 300◦, 330◦. [A1] The other route on the sheet is to take square roots directly: 4 cos2(2θ) = 1 [M1] gives cos 2θ = ±1/2. In one full turn of 2θ this gives 60◦, 120◦, 240◦, 300◦. [A1] Include the second turn, then halve to obtain the eight angles above: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 8 is 12 marks.</p>"
    ],
