    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-o/q9",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q9-question-1.svg\" alt=\"It is known that the cubic equation below has a root α , which is close to 1.25. 3 x + x = 3 . Use an iterative formula based on the Newton Raphson method to find the value of α , correct to 6 decimal places. ( ) 7\" style=\"--madas-width:584.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q9-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"For F(x) = x3 + x −3, F ′(x) = 3x2 + 1. The iteration rule is xn+1 = xn −F(xn)/F ′(xn). Combine the fractions; the numerator is xn(3x2 n + 1) −(x3 n + xn −3) = 3x3 n + xn −x3 n −xn + 3. Newton–Raphson gives xn+1 = xn −x3 n + xn −3 3x2n + 1 [B1] = 2x3 n + 3 3x2n + 1. From x1 = 1.25, [A1] the next values are 1.214285714, 1.213412176, 1.213411663, with the following iterate unchanged to the digits shown: [A1] For verification, F(1.2134115) &lt; 0 &lt; F(1.2134125), [A1] and F ′ &gt; 0.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q9-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Thus α = 1.213412 [A1] to six decimal places: [A1] The handwritten final line truncates the value. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 9 is 7 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "It is known that the cubic equation below has a root α , which is close to 1.25. 3 x + x = 3 . Use an iterative formula based on the Newton Raphson method to find the value of α , correct to 6 decimal places. ( ) 7"
