    "id": "madas/alevel-pure-o/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The curve C has equation ln y y = , y &gt; 0 . x − y Show that the equation of the tangent to C at the point where y = e can be written as ( ) ( 10 ) e x − y = . 1\" style=\"--madas-width:592.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Multiply through and collect terms: y = ln y x −y xy −y2 = ln y xy = y2 + ln y Rearrange to x = y + (ln y)/y. [M1] [A1] At y = e, the point is (e + e−1, e), as ln e = 1. Differentiate using the quotient rule: y × 1 y −ln y × 1 dx dy = 1 + y2 dx dy = 1 + 1 −ln y y2 dx = 1 + 1 −ln e = 1 + 1 −1 = 1 e2 e2 dy y=e\" style=\"--madas-width:565.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-o/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Hence, at this point, dx dy = 1 + 1 −ln y y2 [M1] [M1] [A1] = 1. The tangent has gradient 1, giving y −e = x −e −e−1 [M1] [A1] and then e(x −y) = 1 . [M1] [M1] [A1] Alternative working. For implicit differentiation multiply through by x −y, giving xy −y2 = ln y. At y = e, e(x −e) = 1 gives x = e + e−1. Differentiating with respect to x gives xy′ + y −2yy′ = y′/y. At the point P = (e + e−1, e), this is (e + e−1)y′ + e −2ey′ = y′/e, so collecting the derivative terms yields e = (1/e + 2e −e −1/e)y′, or e = ey′ and y′ = 1. The tangent through P again gives e(x −y) = 1.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 10 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The curve C has equation ln y y = , y > 0 . x − y Show that the equation of the tangent to C at the point where y = e can be written as ( ) ( 10 ) e x − y = . 1"
  },
